      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Shifting from SMS-based 2FA to hardware security keys significantly reduces the risk of interception and eavesdropping due to the physical presence of the user's device. Unlike SMS, where interceptors can simply mimic the verification code, hardware keys require the user to physically authenticate the code, making it much more difficult for attackers to intercept and replicate the verification process. According to studies, encryption weaknesses in SMS-based systems have facilitated nation-state attacks and breaches, whereas hardware keys mitigate these risks.",
